# FRONT SQUAT

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Front Squat is a bilateral lower-body compound exercise performed with the barbell positioned on the anterior shoulders.

Within CAS, it is considered a foundational exercise for developing lower-body strength while emphasizing trunk stability, upright posture and force production through the quadriceps.

---

# Philosophy

The Front Squat prioritizes movement quality over maximal loading.

Compared with the Back Squat, it requires greater postural control, thoracic extension and anterior core stability.

CAS selects the Front Squat when upright force production transfers more effectively to the athlete's sport than maximal absolute loading.

